{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"mcr.microsoft.com/cbl-mariner/base/telegraf","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:12:11.394Z","source":{"name":"Microsoft Artifact Registry","api":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/api/v1/catalog/cbl-mariner/base/telegraf/details?reg=mar","page":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/en-us/product/cbl-mariner/base/telegraf/about"},"readme":"***Warning: Azure Linux 2.0 will reach its End of Life (EOL) on July 31st, 2025. After this date, it will no longer receive updates, security patches, or support, which could leave your systems vulnerable. We strongly recommend upgrading to an Azure Linux 3.0 image before July 31st, 2025.***\n\n## About\n\nThis repository contains the official Telegraf image for CBL-Mariner.\n\n### What is CBL-Mariner?\n\nCBL-Mariner is an internal Linux distribution for Microsoft’s cloud infrastructure and edge products and services. CBL-Mariner is designed to provide a consistent platform for these devices and services and will enhance Microsoft’s ability to stay current on Linux updates.  \n\nTo learn more about CBL-Mariner, refer to our [GitHub repository](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/).\n\n### What is Telegraf?\n\nTelegraf is a server-based agent for collecting and sending all metrics and events from databases, systems, and IoT sensors.\n\nSee: [influxdata.com/time-series-platform/telegraf/](https://www.influxdata.com/time-series-platform/telegraf/)\n\n## Featured tags\n\n- `1`\n- `1-cm2.0`\n\nThe featured tags are multi-architecture tags (i.e., `x86-64` and `aarch64`) that refer to the latest version of the image. Additional tags that are specific to telegraf version, Mariner build, or architecture can be found in the Tags section.\n\n## Configuration\n\nTelegraf can be configured using a mix of a config file, environment variables, and CLI options. If you need to get a config file, once your database / output is configured and is running you can use this command to get it using telegraf CLI shipped with the container:\n\n    telegraf config <options> > telegraf.conf\n\nFor more configuration information refer to [Get Started - Configuration](https://docs.influxdata.com/telegraf/v1/get-started/#configure-telegraf))\n\n## Usage\n\n### Start a telegraf instance\n\n    docker run --name telegraf-logging -d mcr.microsoft.com/cbl-mariner/base/telegraf:1\n\nThe default container startup command is `telegraf`.\n\n ### Launch Mariner shell\n\nThe telegraf image ships with a bash shell. The launch command can be provided to docker run command to launch Mariner shell. The following command will launch the shell:\n\n    docker run -it mcr.microsoft.com/cbl-mariner/base/telegraf:1 /bin/bash\n\nIf you have a config file ready, or need access to ports in the container, the following example shows both in action:\n\n    docker run -it -p 8080:8080 --mount type=bind,source=<path to file>/telegraf.conf,target=/telegraf.conf mcr.microsoft.com/cbl-mariner/base/telegraf:1 /bin/bash\n\n## Support\n\nCBL-Mariner container images are supported only for internal Microsoft use. For more information please see our [Support Statement](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/blob/2.0/SUPPORT.md).\n\n## License\n\nThe CBL-Mariner distribution is provided under the [MIT license](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/blob/2.0/LICENSE). Individual packages and components are governed by their own licenses included in the package sources available via srpm on [packages.microsoft.com](https://packages.microsoft.com/cbl-mariner/) or via our [GitHub repository](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/).\n\n- Legal Notice: [Container License Information](https://aka.ms/mcr/osslegalnotice)","readmeBase":null,"publisher":{"name":"Microsoft","url":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/","official":true,"verified":true},"registered":null,"updated":"2026-07-21T16:57:12.5633836+00:00","categories":[],"keywords":[],"license":"MIT","links":[],"maintainers":[],"stats":{"pulls":null,"pullsText":"127K+","stars":null},"mediaTypes"